WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.444
Week six.

00:00:01.494 --> 00:00:06.144
Managing a brand for social purpose, with Libby Hogson from UNICEF Australia.

00:00:06.733 --> 00:00:09.362
There are over sixty thousand Australian charities.

00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:10.723
One for every four hundred and thirty nine people.

00:00:10.773 --> 00:00:14.277
And fewer donors are giving more.

00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:17.830
In twenty twenty UNICEF had zero unprompted awareness.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.688
Yet about ninety five percent of spend went on conversion,

00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:22.440
and five percent on awareness.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.571
The top of the funnel was empty.

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:28.242
Top of mind, donation intent is nineteen percent.

00:00:28.292 --> 00:00:30.162
Only prompted, it's seven.

00:00:30.212 --> 00:00:33.071
Mental availability nearly triples intent.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:34.822
So the positioning:

00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:38.807
UNICEF inspires Australians with the determination it takes to protect every child,

00:00:38.857 --> 00:00:39.878
no matter what.

00:00:39.928 --> 00:00:42.171
Then say it again and again.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.213
Then measure the chain.

00:00:44.263 --> 00:00:47.137
Ad awareness and share of voice drive unprompted awareness,

00:00:47.187 --> 00:00:48.308
then donation intent,

00:00:48.358 --> 00:00:49.759
then market share.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.444
The takeaway?

00:00:51.494 --> 00:00:53.955
Brand building in a charity is brand building.

00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:56.807
Stay the course, and measure everything.
